Defend a source assessment and its limits (@wu-source-review: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #water-and-sanitation "../treatment/Translate-raw-water-variation-into-treatment-questions.lingua#r_3M5Z05Q30W6P11QVNY3BF6ZZRS") { r_2TB6K13XR13MWGGQC401ZJA732
**Read:** Complete [Groundwater Resource Development](../sources/Groundwater-resource-development.lingua#r_1M3NS4Y0CV4391JF136S20MVBP), including chapter 8 and the case studies; use [EPA source-water assessment](../sources/Source-water-assessment-EPA.lingua#r_5T76MTRS1XYC431J6XFG5B7FME) and [WHO/IWA water safety plan manual](../sources/Water-Safety-Plan-Manual-WHO.lingua#r_3JMZKS3FG80FKX9YRQPEJMA4VD) to critique your source assessment. Work the groundwater exercises before comparing solutions and document any model or software dependencies separately from the book.

Assemble a source assessment for a documented location or a clearly labelled synthetic case. Include a boundary map, chronological quantity account, alternative source models, quality evidence, protection proposal, observation programme and assumptions about energy and maintenance. Compare surface water, groundwater and a mixed option. Explain why mean annual volume, a well test or one compliant sample cannot alone prove continuing service.

Supply calculations another reader can reproduce. Retain initial conditions and time conventions; close water and constituent balances; test drought, common-cause failure and source-quality interruption. Show which conclusion survives changed assumptions and which depends on an unverified parameter. Separate modelled availability from permissions, ecological limits and treatment capability.

For deeper study, reproduce one published case or analytical exercise, compare a second explanation, and use withheld observations or an independent calculation to test it. Discuss identifiability, discretization where applicable, and what would falsify the model. A polished fit is not evidence of unique parameters or a reliable forecast.

**Completion for this section:** Explain the source to a newcomer, defend its quantitative account to a critical reader, and identify observations that could overturn the recommendation. The next section must translate the resulting raw-water envelope into treatment barriers and operating evidence. Source assessment does not complete treatment design, sanitation, industrial utilities or the wider water trail.

**Water treatment continuation:** [Translate raw-water variation into treatment questions](../treatment/Translate-raw-water-variation-into-treatment-questions.lingua#r_3M5Z05Q30W6P11QVNY3BF6ZZRS).
